<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marciano returns two weeks after intake and was seen this morning by Dr. Achterberg-Lund of sports medicine. The pain down his left leg now comes only after sitting for an hour, and the numbness on the top of his left foot is less. His back aches at about 5 out of 10, stiff in the morning. He took naproxen twice a day for the first week and now takes it once a day after walking, with food, with no stomach upset. He uses the gel on his left thumb three times a day, and gripping is still sore. He took his blood pressure at home twice a day for a week as shown, and the average was 126/78 mmHg. He walks for an hour each morning and has not run or hit the bag. He has eaten smaller portions and his weight is down by 0.4 kg. He has no headaches, memory trouble or problems with balance, and is sleeping better than he was at intake. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Back pain</td><td>5 out of 10; leg pain only after long sitting</td></tr><tr><td>Thumb pain</td><td>5 out of 10; grip 38 kg left and 54 kg right; FIHOA 9 out of 30</td></tr><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Average 126/78 mmHg over seven days</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>91.6 kg, from 92.0</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

